---
system: sys-01-identity-household-access
flow_id: password-reset
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/01-identity-household-access#4-3-post-v1authforgot-password
actors: [ParentApp, Gateway, IdentityService, SES]
apis:
  - POST /v1/auth/forgot-password
externals: [SES]
queues: [auth.email]
failure_paths:
  - auth_password_reset_rate_limited
  - ses_send_failed
idempotency: server-side dedup by email within 1h rate-limit window — endpoint always returns 200 regardless of account existence to prevent account enumeration
retry: caller-side single retry on 5xx — never retry on 200 (would re-trigger email)
timeout: 5s p99
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. Account-enumeration defense: always 200, even when email is unknown. Reset link only delivered if account exists.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant IdentityService
    participant SES

    ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/auth/forgot-password {email}
    Gateway->>Gateway: rate-limit (sys-17) — auth_password_reset — 3 per hour per email
    Gateway->>IdentityService: forward request
    alt auth_password_reset_rate_limited
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 429 auth_password_reset_rate_limited
    else account unknown
        Note over IdentityService: silent — no email sent, no log of email-not-found leak
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {message: "If that email exists, a reset link has been sent."}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    else account exists
        IdentityService-)SES: (async via queue auth.email) password-reset email with one-time token
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {message: "If that email exists, a reset link has been sent."}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    end

    Note over ParentApp,SES: response identical for known and unknown email — timeout 5s p99 — SES failures handled async (no impact on caller response)
